1
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:43,500
Based on the untold true story

2
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:21,000
Outlaw King is a action, history, war film directed by David Mackenzie.

3
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:58,500
Forced into exile by the English after being crowned King of Scotland,
legendary warrior Robert the Bruce fights to reclaim the throne.

4
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:36,000
Robert Bruce, Earl of Carrick, played by Chris Pine.

5
00:38:07,500 --> 00:38:13,500
James Douglas, Lord of Douglas, played by Aaron Taylor-Johnson.

6
00:45:45,000 --> 00:45:51,000
Elizabeth Burgh, played by Florence Pugh.

7
00:53:22,500 --> 00:53:28,500
Edward, Prince of Wales, played by Billy Howle.

8
01:01:00,000 --> 01:01:06,000
Aymer de Valence, Earl of Pembroke, played by Sam Spruell.

9
01:08:37,500 --> 01:08:43,500
Angus Og Macdonald, Lord of Islay, played by Tony Curran.

10
01:16:15,000 --> 01:16:21,000
Outlaw King is a 2018 historical action drama film,
co-written, produced, and directed by David Mackenzie.

11
01:23:52,500 --> 01:23:58,500
Chris Pine stars as Scottish king Robert the Bruce during
the Scottish Wars of Independence in 1304–07.

12
01:31:30,000 --> 01:31:36,000
The ensemble cast also features Aaron Taylor-Johnson, Florence Pugh, Billy Howle, Sam
Spruell, Tony Curran, Callan Mulvey, James Cosmo and Stephen Dillane.

13
01:39:07,500 --> 01:39:13,500
Outlaw King premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival on September 6,
2018, and was released on streaming on November 9 by Netflix.

14
01:46:45,000 --> 01:46:51,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics, who praised its production design, sets,
performances, and choreography, but criticised its historical inaccuracies and clichés.

15
01:54:22,500 --> 01:54:28,500
The film explores themes of scotland, castle,
exile, biography, based on true story.
